An Echo Fragment is a piece of something that no longer exists, embodied well enough to be carried. Holding one gives what it holds and burns away the rest, so a bearer needs power enough to survive it; the fragment tears the whole of that bearer's life out of the world's record, and no one can say who they were. What stands three times removed from a life is not counted part of it, and survives the tearing.

The [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|Stranger]] held one at the centre of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]. He took it from its previous holder, [[People/Althane/Karen Sill|Karen Sill]], laying a hand on the bound man's face. An echo of a bearer's life can be watched, and by it the name the fragment tore away may be learned. The Weft killed the Stranger and the fragment went with him.

[[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech of Sedecium]] hunted another, holding that its removal changes nothing for the world. They took it up. It gave them the one thing they had wanted all along: it made them a god, and it tore them out of every record, so that no one remembers them. The pavilion of statues at [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] counts three where it once counted four.
